From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 00:00:47 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: imx8mq-phanbell: Supply the PCIe PHY VPH rail

LDO7 feeds PCIE_VPH on both controllers, at 3.3V. The driver needs to
know that: pci-imx6.c clears IMX8MQ_GPR_PCIE_VREG_BYPASS when the vph
regulator reads above 3V, because the datasheet expects PCIE_VPH to be
1.8V and the internal regulator has to be taken out of bypass when it
is not.

Without the property the supply is simply absent, the check never runs
and the PHY is left in bypass with a 3.3V VPH. The vendor devicetree
carries vph-supply on both ports for the same reason.

Signed-off-by: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts
index 71863c4..d7d6b1e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/freescale/imx8mq-phanbell.dts
@@ -376,6 +376,7 @@
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	pinctrl-0 = <&pinctrl_pcie0>;
 	reset-gpio = <&gpio3 10 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+	vph-supply = <&ldo7>;
 	/*
 	 * pcie0 takes REF_CLK from the internal PLL, and the SoC drives the
 	 * 100 MHz reference out to the endpoint on CLK2_P/N. That output is
@@ -396,6 +397,7 @@
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	pinctrl-0 = <&pinctrl_pcie1>;
 	reset-gpio = <&gpio3 18 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+	vph-supply = <&ldo7>;
 	clocks = <&clk IMX8MQ_CLK_PCIE2_ROOT>,
 		 <&pcie1_refclk>,
 		 <&clk IMX8MQ_CLK_PCIE2_PHY>,
